cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Gridrich, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Gridrich: grid-based species occurrence and richness analysis from occurrence records in the browser"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Chakma
    given-names: Kakon
    affiliation: "Conservation Ecology Laboratory, School of Environment and Sustainability, University of Saskatchewan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kakonck/gridrich"
url: "https://github.com/kakonck/gridrich"
keywords:
  - species richness
  - occurrence data
  - spatial grid
  - biodiversity informatics
  - GBIF
  - rarefaction
abstract: "Gridrich divides a study area into equal-area square or hexagonal grid cells of one or several sizes and into user-supplied regions, and reports occurrence counts, observed species richness, record density, rarefied richness, species frequency, presence/absence and compositional similarity, with maps, charts, a methods statement and exports. It runs entirely in the web browser."
